# eOn SVN r2549. HarnessCounter through ext_pot. Kernel morse_pt.
# Climbing-image NEB, same stops as eon/neb-pt-lbfgs. Eight images, L-BFGS memory 20, max_move 0.2, max_iterations 1000, converged_force 0.01. The harness cap is 10000. force_calls is the harness total across the band. Potential morse_pt. r2549 does not read energy_weighted, ci_mmf, climbing_image_band_slack, setup_mmf_peaks, or the develop L-BFGS catalog past memory, inverse curvature, max inverse curvature, auto scale, and the two resets. Those keys are omitted. The keys it does read sit in [Optimizer]. The run swaps the potential for ext_pot. The harness kernel is the develop kernel for this potential name. morse_pt here is r2549 Morse::force: cutoff 9.5, pair energy shifted to zero at the cutoff, minimum image on the box diagonal. The develop harness Morse has no cutoff and ignores the box, and that form ends every Pt saddle search above max_energy 5. The 2014 table used r2090. The binary is SVN r2549, the registry pin. Export of the 2014 revision is forbidden, so this row is r2549.
# Each start is the mean of 2 replicates (svn-all and fortran). n is the number of distinct starts. 0 starts differ in force_calls. Success agrees on every start.
counter harness
code Eon svn
code_version r2549
commit r2549
algorithm LBFGS
tuning default
template eon-svn/neb-pt-ci
problem neb/Pt-heptamer
reducer harness
cap 10000
n 13
par2_mean 336.7692307692308
nfailed 0
mean_calls 336.7692307692308
median_calls 338.0
min_calls 218.0
max_calls 442.0
n_crash 0
n_divergence 0
n_cap 0
n_wrong_stationary 0
n_replicates 2
n_differing 0
success_rate 1.0
wilson_low 0.7719046276458016
wilson_high 1.0
